  "body": "The Providers tab rendered every provider as one flat field grid in catalog order: **76 visible inputs**, no grouping, no search, and a provider's key, base URL and proxy scattered across the same undifferentiated grid rather than sitting together. Tolerable at 12 providers; not at 35.\n\n## What replaces it\n\nEach provider gets a **card** carrying its own status pill, credential env name and its own fields — including a per-card \"Advanced options\" fold for proxy and base URL, instead of one section-wide advanced toggle that revealed everything at once.\n\nCards sit in **collapsible groups** driven by the catalog metadata added in 4.38.0: coding plans, model providers, inference platforms, gateways, local runtimes, custom. Each group summary carries a configured count and a rail of status dots that double as jump links.\n\nAbove them: a **search box** matching display name, provider id, credential env var and base URL, plus a **Configured only** toggle. Searching `alibaba` narrows 35 cards to 4.\n\n**Ordering answers the common question first.** Configured providers sort to the top of their group, then missing-key, then unknown. The first group with anything configured opens by default, so the page never lands fully collapsed with no way in.\n\nThe separate provider status strip is **gone** — it was a second place to read the same status. Now every card carries its own pill.\n\n**Web Search** gets the search box and the same filter, and nothing else. Ten providers already rendered as cards there; a second card system would have been change for its own sake.\n\n## Filtering hides, never detaches — this is load-bearing\n\n`changedValues()` finds fields by walking `[data-key]` across the document. An input removed while filtered would silently stop being saveable — the exact defect that made fallback chains unusable from 4.31.0 until 4.34.1. So filtering sets the `hidden` attribute, which also removes the element from the tab order, so a filtered-out card cannot trap keyboard focus.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe two failures this area has already shipped — a detached input and an unstyled class — are invisible to every check in this repo. So both were tested directly rather than reasoned about.\n\n`admin.js` was **executed in jsdom** against the real 296-field admin payload:\n\n```\nPASS  every provider field is in the document        76 provider inputs\nPASS  provider groups render                         5 groups\nPASS  provider cards render                          35 cards\nPASS  filtering hides but never detaches inputs      all 76 inputs still in document while filtered\n                                                     | visible cards: 4\nPASS  all admin views exist                          7 views\nPASS  no uncaught script errors                      clean\n```\n\nRun against unmodified `main` as a **positive control**, the same harness reports `0 groups`, `0 cards` and \"no search input found\" — which is what makes the result above mean anything. One check fails **identically on both** (45 diagnostics/smoke fields whose sections map to no view container), so it is pre-existing, not a regression.\n\nThe `pv-` prefix is registered with `test_admin_static_styles_every_class_the_script_emits`, so an unstyled class in the new markup now fails loudly.\n\n```\nruff format / ruff check / ty: clean\npytest tests/api/test_admin.py: 72 passed\n```\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **None of this has been rendered in a browser.** There was no browser tooling in this session. jsdom proves structure, wiring and the DOM invariants; it says nothing about how any of it *looks*. The three things most likely to need a second pass: spacing/density inside a card, the dot rail at ~10 dots, and the card grid at narrow widths.\n- The group taxonomy is a judgement call. NVIDIA NIM is filed under \"Inference platforms\" rather than \"Model providers\"; Ollama Cloud likewise. Reasonable people could file those differently — it is one line in the catalog to move.\n- Group summary counts do not update while a filter is active; they always describe the unfiltered group.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
