    "message": "feat(admin): make 35 providers findable — grouped, searchable provider cards\n\nThe Providers tab rendered every provider as one flat field grid in catalog\norder: 76 visible inputs, no grouping, no search, and a provider's key, base\nURL and proxy scattered across the same undifferentiated grid rather than\nsitting together. That was tolerable at 12 providers and stopped being so\nsomewhere around 30. It is now 35.\n\nWhat replaces it. Each provider gets a card carrying its own status pill,\ncredential env name and its own fields, including a per-card \"Advanced\noptions\" fold for proxy and base URL rather than one section-wide advanced\ntoggle. Cards sit in collapsible groups driven by the catalog metadata added\nin 4.38.0 -- coding plans, model providers, inference platforms, gateways,\nlocal runtimes, custom -- and each group summary carries a configured count\nand a rail of status dots that double as jump links into the group.\n\nAbove them, a search box that matches on display name, provider id,\ncredential env var and base URL, plus a \"Configured only\" toggle. Searching\n\"alibaba\" narrows 35 cards to 4.\n\nOrdering answers the common question first: configured providers sort to the\ntop of their group, then missing-key, then unknown. The first group with\nanything configured opens by default, so the page never lands fully\ncollapsed with no way in.\n\nThe separate provider status strip is gone. It was a second place to read\nthe same status, and now that every card carries its own pill there is one.\n\nFiltering hides with the `hidden` attribute and never detaches. That is\nload-bearing, not incidental: `changedValues()` finds fields by walking\n[data-key] across the document, so an input removed while filtered would\nsilently stop being saveable -- the exact defect that made fallback chains\nunusable from 4.31.0 to 4.34.1. `hidden` also takes an element out of the\ntab order, so a filtered-out card cannot trap keyboard focus.\n\nWeb Search gets the search box and the same hide-don't-detach filter, and\nnothing else. Ten providers already rendered as cards there; a second card\nsystem would have been change for its own sake.\n\nVerification. The two failures this area has already shipped -- a detached\ninput and an unstyled class -- are both invisible to every check in this\nrepo, so both were tested directly rather than reasoned about.\n\nadmin.js was executed in jsdom against the real 296-field admin payload:\n\n  5 groups render, 35 provider cards render\n  all 76 provider inputs present in the document\n  filtering to \"alibaba\" -> 4 visible cards, 0 inputs detached\n  no uncaught script errors\n  all 7 admin views still render (the VIEW_GROUPS null-container trap)\n\nRun against unmodified main as a positive control, the same harness reports\n0 groups and 0 cards and finds no search input, which is what makes the\nabove mean something. One check fails identically on both -- 45 diagnostics\nand smoke fields whose sections map to no view container -- so it is\npre-existing, not a regression.\n\nThe `pv-` prefix is registered with test_admin_static_styles_every_class_\nthe_script_emits, so an unstyled class in the new markup now fails loudly.\n\n  ruff format / ruff check / ty: clean\n  pytest tests/api/test_admin.py: 72 passed\n\nNot done: none of this has been rendered in a browser. There was no browser\ntooling in this session. jsdom proves structure, wiring and the DOM\ninvariants; it says nothing about how any of it looks. Spacing, the dot\nrail's density at 10 dots, and the card grid at narrow widths are the three\nthings most likely to need a second pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
